    "summary": "Tesla's XBRL filings contain two revenue concepts because the SEC taxonomy added a newer concept for revenue from contracts with customers excluding assessed taxes after the ASC 606 update, while retaining the legacy 'Revenues' concept for total GAAP revenue. In the available data, only the 'Revenues' concept appears with values; the second concept is present in the taxonomy but has no reported values in the sampled periods.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Tesla's XBRL taxonomy includes both 'Revenues' and 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' concepts.",
        "evidence": ["E-50d25e"]
      },
      {
        "text": "For every fiscal year and period in the sample (2011‑2023), Tesla's filings report numeric values only under the 'Revenues' concept; no rows show a value for 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax'.",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d"]
      }
    ],
    "inferences": [
      {
        "text": "The dual concepts likely stem from the SEC's adoption of ASC 606, which introduced the newer concept for contract revenue while keeping the legacy concept for total GAAP revenue.",
        "basis": ["Claim about both concepts existing", "General knowledge of ASC 606 taxonomy changes"]
      },
      {
        "text": "To obtain Tesla's total GAAP revenue, use the 'Revenues' concept for all years; to analyze core contract revenue excluding assessed taxes, use the newer concept where it is reported (likely from FY 2018 onward).",
        "basis": ["Claim about both concepts existing", "Inference about ASC 606"]
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis_verdicts": [
      {
        "id": "H-8edb42",
        "status": "supported",
        "evidence": ["E-50d25e", "E-01109d"],
        "why": "Both concepts exist in the taxonomy and the legacy concept continues to be used throughout the sample, consistent with a taxonomy version switch."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-8348d9",
        "status": "refuted",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d"],
        "why": "No fiscal period shows both concepts with values; thus duplicate amended filings are not evident in the data."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-df72bc",
